  "faithful": "This remark is important: for many carpenters think the form and direction of the butting joint of great importance; and even the theorist, by not prosecuting the general principle through all its consequences, may be led into an error. The form of the joint is of no importance, in as far as it affects the strains in the direction of the beams; but it is often of great consequence, in respect to its own firmness, and the effect it may have in bruising the piece on which it acts, or being crippled by it.",
